// "<agent> faces a villainous choice — <A>, or <B>" [CR#701.55a]: "means
// '<agent> chooses <A> or <B>. Then all actions in the chosen option are
// performed.'" No dedicated Lean `semantic_macro` exists for this shape yet
// (absent from `lean/Semantics/Macros.lean`); the general
// `Instruction::ChooseModes` core constructor Lean's own `chooseModes`
// wraps is the intended shape (`quantity := exactly 1`, no costs, two
// modes), per `lean/Semantics/Check/Facts.lean`'s "Face A Villainous Choice"
// row.
//
// STOP (updated by `semantics-v2-macro-param-kinds`): the two options are
// `Instruction`s. `deckmaste_semantics_v2::ron::param_types()` now has that
// param type (this ticket's crate fix), but `deckmaste_construction_core::
// macro_def::ParameterType` — the SAME closed eight-name enum, mirrored
// independently on the english_v2/typed side that reads every `plugins_v2`
// declaration's `params:` field too (§11: neither crate depends on the
// other for the shared declaration file, so BOTH readers must accept a
// param type before any declaration can use it) — has no `Instruction`
// variant and was out of this ticket's authorized file scope. A one-sided
// fix is unusable (`both_readers_accept_every_builtin_declaration` fails
// from the construction_core side alone). Left bodyless pending that
// companion fix.
KeywordAction(
    name: "FaceAVillainousChoice",
    spelling: "face a villainous choice",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "face a villainous choice",
        third_person: "faces a villainous choice",
        frame_set: Intransitive,
    ),
)
